                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Test yourself before checking the answers."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "1. Which test records electrical activity directly from skeletal muscle?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Nerve conduction study only"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Needle EMG"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Pulse oximetry"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "2. Which pattern is more typical of a myopathic process?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Small, short-duration motor-unit potentials with early recruitment"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Large, long-duration potentials with reduced recruitment"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Prolonged nerve latency alone"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "3. Which statement about fasciculation potentials is correct?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "They prove motor neuron disease"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "They can occur in several conditions and require clinical interpretation"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "They are always a normal finding"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "electromyograph_emg_group_20",
